Answer: A basic Java program contains a class, a main() method, and a statement such as System.out.println() to print output on the console.

```java
class Demo {
public static void main(String[] args) {
System.out.println("Namaskara Karnataka");
}
}
```

The logic to be executed is placed inside the main() method, and the main() method is placed inside the class.

Answer: A simple Java program can be written as:

```java
class Demo {
public static void main(String[] args) {
System.out.println("Hello");
}
}
```

The class contains the main() method, and the System.out.println() statement prints the message.

Answer: The array brackets can be placed in different positions. Examples include:

```java
public static void main(String[] args)
public static void main(String args[])
```

Both forms are valid.
